# [T15-BE-DOCKER][REQ-2] What never enters the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named paths rather than `.`, so most of this is
# belt-and-braces for context size and build speed. Two entries are about
# correctness and are the reason this file exists at all:
#
#   .env          manage.py reads DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE out of it. A laptop's
#                 .env baked into the image would make `manage.py migrate`
#                 inside a container silently run under dev settings.
#   .venv/        the laptop's virtualenv is the wrong interpreter's, and it
#                 is the largest thing in the directory.
#
# tests/ is deliberately NOT listed. The `test` build target copies it; the
# `runtime` target simply never asks for it.

# --- Secrets and local configuration ---------------------------------------
.env
.env.*

# --- Interpreter and caches --------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# --- Generated at build or run time, never copied in --------------------------
# collectstatic runs inside the build; a laptop's staticfiles/ would be the
# wrong settings module's output (see the Plan B troubleshooting table).
staticfiles/
# Uploads are state. They live on a volume or in S3, never in an image.
media/

# --- Test output ---------------------------------------------------------------
test-reports/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
junit.xml

# --- Not part of the application -----------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
